# Contributor Covenant Code of Conduct

## Our Pledge
We pledge to make participation in our project a harassment-free experience for everyone, regardless of age, body size, disability, ethnicity, gender identity and expression, level of experience, nationality, personal appearance, race, religion, or sexual identity and orientation.

## Our Standards
Examples of behavior that contributes to a positive environment include:
- Being respectful and considerate.
- Using welcoming and inclusive language.
- Accepting constructive criticism gracefully.
- Focusing on what is best for the community.

Examples of unacceptable behavior include harassment, insults, discrimination, and publishing others' private information without permission.

## Enforcement Responsibilities
Project maintainers are responsible for clarifying and enforcing our standards of acceptable behavior.

## Scope
This Code of Conduct applies within project spaces and whenever someone represents the project or its community.

## Enforcement
Unacceptable behavior may be reported to the project maintainers. They may take appropriate and fair corrective action, including warnings or temporary or permanent exclusion from the project.

## Enforcement Guidelines
Maintainers will review reports fairly, consistently, and confidentially, and will take action appropriate to the circumstances.

